    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the September 4 slate with a clear objective: maximize stolen base upside and exploit favorable platoon splits to close the gap in 5x5 Roto. **Yordan Alvarez** (87.42) anchors the lineup as our premier start, boasting an elite 0.451 xwOBA and a highly favorable matchup against Merrill Kelly, whose 5.23 xERA provides the perfect runway for a massive offensive night. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12) is our second-most efficient play; batting atop the order against Janson Junk offers an ideal environment for his speed profile to impact both the R and SB categories simultaneously. **Christian Yelich** (74.33) also projects as an elite-tier option, as Rhett Lowder\u2019s pitching style combined with a significant dynamic platoon advantage makes him a high-floor start for our roster.\n\nStrategic platoon advantages are driving much of the lower-middle order\u2019s value today. **Caleb Durbin** (68.17) and **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) benefit heavily from park factors and platoon alignments, providing the depth needed to sustain offensive momentum. Meanwhile, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (63.44) remains a must-start due to his ability to leverage the park and platoon edge against Ranger Suarez. Among our bench options, **Jacob Gonzalez** (50.42) was the final man left out; despite a favorable 5.35 xERA matchup against Ryan Johnson, his projected spot at the bottom of the order (-6% penalty) ultimately cost him a starting role against the current utility options. \n\nRisk management remains critical as we navigate \"Lineup Pending\" designations for nearly the entire roster. **Trea Turner** (54.22) faces a heightened challenge against the elite Chris Sale; while his 2.79 xERA makes this a tough outing, **Trea Turner** remains locked in due to his unique stolen base floor. Additionally, we are closely monitoring the status of **Gary Sanchez**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, all of whom hold sub-60 scores. Should their official lineups move them further down the order, we may reconsider their deployment to preserve game caps, particularly since **Dillon Dingler** and **Carson Benge** are already sitting on the razor-thin margin of our 40-59 \"Marginal\" threshold.",
